{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T12:45:35.116Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The task is the classic `x_or_y` prime test. I’ll use trial division up to the square root: it handles all integer inputs, including negatives, 0, and 1, without imports. For the proof, the key is a generalized loop claim over an arbitrary divisor; that gives K a genuine circular invariant instead of reducing the verification to only the two examples.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T12:45:35.116Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0db710fe2b465b53016a60bb6cb9748194929a3afe399ec22e","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The task is the classic `x_or_y` prime test. I’ll use trial division up to the square root: it handles all integer inputs, including negatives, 0, and 1, without imports. For the proof, the key is a generalized loop claim over an arbitrary divisor; that gives K a genuine circular invariant instead of reducing the verification to only the two examples."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f89da-b557-76c0-9059-932670e3aa9c"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T12:45:38.097Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0db710fe2b465b53016a60bb6f19408194b710be1740958944","status":"completed","call_id":"call_O88wBja73WMIqAbnSTO3M6B4","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /work/solution.py\\n+def x_or_y(n, x, y):\\n+    if n < 2:\\n+        return y\\n+    divisor = 2\\n+    while divisor * divisor <= n:\\n+        if n % divisor == 0:\\n+            return y\\n+        divisor = divisor + 1\\n+    return x\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\nconst r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 py2mpy.py solution.py > solution.mpy && sed -n '1,240p' solution.mpy && python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom solution import x_or_y\\ncases = [(7,34,12,34),(15,8,5,5),(-3,1,2,2),(0,1,2,2),(1,1,2,2),(2,1,2,1),(3,1,2,1),(4,1,2,2),(97,11,22,11),(121,11,22,22)]\\nfor n,x,y,want in cases:\\n    got=x_or_y(n,x,y)\\n    assert got == want, (n,got,want)\\nprint('python smoke tests passed:', len(cases))\\nPY\",\"workdir\":\"/work\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000});\ntext(r.output);","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f89da-b557-76c0-9059-932670e3aa9c"}}}
